 'The current chip definition is sound introductory naming content. Its shared sy0701.term.soc support node and case-insensitive glossary collision with Security Operations Center remain held; no text replacement or node split.',
 'The existing APK/adware example remains an illustrative malicious case. Legitimate off-store enterprise/developer distribution defeats the current universal untrusted-source implication. The authored attack cardType, deck placement and attack-name captions remain unchanged and require separate review; no installation is performed.',
 'The current definition soundly identifies a security challenge format. It does not teach privacy/compliance or establish the inherited governance placement, training effectiveness, mastery or a precise objective.',
 'The current definition soundly identifies a connectivity provider. Supplier assurance, service obligations, resilience and privacy/compliance are not taught merely by the name; placement remains held.',
 'This proposes an explicit study grouping, not universal legal equivalence or a binding/nonbinding rule. An owner must still approve the intended usage; no agreement, payment authority or legal effect is assessed.',
 'The current definition is sound naming vocabulary in its technical examples. Identifier assignment does not prove certificate trust, security authority or relevance to governance/compliance; placement remains held.',
 'Reuse the exact earlier offline PHI glossary candidate with a separate card binding. Identifiable health information alone does not establish HIPAA scope, and defined exclusions remain relevant. No real records classified.',
